# Sample requests (VS Code REST Client / IntelliJ HTTP client). Run the app first.
@base = http://localhost:8081

### SRP
POST {{base}}/srp/after/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "orderId": "ORD-1", "price": 50, "quantity": 2 }

### OCP — pix only exists in the "after" version
POST {{base}}/ocp/after/payments
Content-Type: application/json

{ "orderId": "ORD-1", "amount": 100, "paymentMethod": "pix" }

### LSP — the same order from two providers. Compare "before" and "after".
GET {{base}}/lsp/before/orders/ORD-1001?provider=legacy

###
GET {{base}}/lsp/before/orders/ORD-1001?provider=new

###
GET {{base}}/lsp/after/orders/ORD-1001?provider=new

### ISP
GET {{base}}/isp/before/orders/ORD-1001

###
GET {{base}}/isp/after/mobile/orders/ORD-1001

###
GET {{base}}/isp/after/finance/orders/ORD-1001

### DIP
GET {{base}}/dip/after/orders/ORD-1001

### EIP idempotent receiver — same order twice: "before" charges it twice, "after" answers 409 the second time
POST {{base}}/eip/payments/after/charges
Content-Type: application/json

{ "orderId": "ORD-2001", "amount": 100 }

###
POST {{base}}/eip/payments/before/charges
Content-Type: application/json

{ "orderId": "ORD-2002", "amount": 100 }

### EIP idempotent receiver — three different orders from one For Each: before gives accepted,duplicate,duplicate
POST {{base}}/eip/payments/before/charges/batch
Content-Type: application/json

[ { "orderId": "ORD-2101", "amount": 10 }, { "orderId": "ORD-2102", "amount": 20 }, { "orderId": "ORD-2103", "amount": 30 } ]

### ...and after accepts all three
POST {{base}}/eip/payments/after/charges/batch
Content-Type: application/json

[ { "orderId": "ORD-2201", "amount": 10 }, { "orderId": "ORD-2202", "amount": 20 }, { "orderId": "ORD-2203", "amount": 30 } ]

### Charges and rejected duplicates for one order
GET {{base}}/eip/payments/ORD-2001/charges

### EIP correlation identifier — status after the provider called back (PAID: the simulated provider always approves; PAYMENT_DECLINED and PAYMENT_REVIEW are produced only by the MUnit tests)
GET {{base}}/eip/payments/ORD-2001/status

### A callback nobody is waiting for (unknown, expired, or a repeat of one already matched): 404
POST {{base}}/eip/payments/callback
Content-Type: application/json

{ "correlationId": "PRQ-UNKNOWN", "status": "APPROVED", "approvedAmount": 1, "providerReference": "PRV-X" }

### Mule correlationId — sent in X-CORRELATION-ID by default, not sent with sendCorrelationId NEVER
GET {{base}}/eip/correlation-id/call/default

###
GET {{base}}/eip/correlation-id/call/never

### EIP content-based router — domestic, international and review (the first matching rule wins: this one goes to review)
POST {{base}}/eip/orders/route
Content-Type: application/json

{ "orderId": "ORD-3001", "country": "BR", "amount": 120, "items": [ { "sku": "SKU-BOOK", "quantity": 1, "unitPrice": 120 } ] }

###
POST {{base}}/eip/orders/route
Content-Type: application/json

{ "orderId": "ORD-3002", "country": "PT", "amount": 120, "items": [ { "sku": "SKU-BOOK", "quantity": 1, "unitPrice": 120 } ] }

###
POST {{base}}/eip/orders/route
Content-Type: application/json

{ "orderId": "ORD-3003", "country": "US", "amount": 5000, "items": [ { "sku": "SKU-BOOK", "quantity": 1, "unitPrice": 5000 } ] }

### EIP message filter — a declined order: "before" answers DISCARDED but reserves stock anyway
POST {{base}}/eip/stock/before/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{ "orderId": "ORD-3101", "status": "PAYMENT_DECLINED", "items": [ { "sku": "SKU-BOOK", "quantity": 2 } ] }

###
GET {{base}}/eip/stock/ORD-3101/reservations

### ...and "after" reserves nothing
POST {{base}}/eip/stock/after/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{ "orderId": "ORD-3102", "status": "PAYMENT_DECLINED", "items": [ { "sku": "SKU-BOOK", "quantity": 2 } ] }

###
GET {{base}}/eip/stock/ORD-3102/reservations

### EIP splitter — the same order with For Each and with Parallel For Each
POST {{base}}/eip/stock/availability/for-each
Content-Type: application/json

{ "orderId": "ORD-3201", "items": [ { "sku": "SKU-BOOK", "quantity": 2 }, { "sku": "SKU-POSTER", "quantity": 1 }, { "sku": "SKU-MUG", "quantity": 3 } ] }

###
POST {{base}}/eip/stock/availability/parallel-for-each
Content-Type: application/json

{ "orderId": "ORD-3201", "items": [ { "sku": "SKU-BOOK", "quantity": 2 }, { "sku": "SKU-POSTER", "quantity": 1 }, { "sku": "SKU-MUG", "quantity": 3 } ] }

### EIP aggregator — the client splits the order and posts its items one by one; the last one gets the invoice
POST {{base}}/eip/invoices/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "orderId": "ORD-3301", "items": [ { "sku": "SKU-BOOK", "quantity": 2, "unitPrice": 30 }, { "sku": "SKU-MUG", "quantity": 1, "unitPrice": 12.5 } ] }

###
GET {{base}}/eip/invoices/ORD-3301

### One item of a two-item order: 202, and after 5 seconds the invoice is INCOMPLETE
POST {{base}}/eip/invoices/items
Content-Type: application/json

{ "orderId": "ORD-3302", "itemCount": 2, "sku": "SKU-BOOK", "quantity": 1, "unitPrice": 30 }

###
GET {{base}}/eip/invoices/ORD-3302

### EIP recipient list — an international order with physical and digital items goes to all four recipients
POST {{base}}/eip/orders/notifications
Content-Type: application/json

{ "orderId": "ORD-3401", "country": "US", "items": [ { "sku": "SKU-BOOK", "quantity": 1, "unitPrice": 30, "type": "PHYSICAL" }, { "sku": "SKU-EBOOK", "quantity": 1, "unitPrice": 9, "type": "DIGITAL" } ] }

###
GET {{base}}/eip/orders/ORD-3401/notifications

### EIP scatter-gather — pricing, stock and fraud checks in parallel (a CUS-NEW... customer goes to REVIEW)
POST {{base}}/eip/orders/checks
Content-Type: application/json

{ "orderId": "ORD-3501", "customerId": "CUS-100", "items": [ { "sku": "SKU-BOOK", "quantity": 2, "unitPrice": 30 }, { "sku": "SKU-MUG", "quantity": 1, "unitPrice": 12.5 } ] }

### EIP message translator — a partner order as CSV becomes this app's order
POST {{base}}/eip/orders/translate
Content-Type: application/csv

partnerOrderRef,buyerCode,shipToCountry,productCode,qty,unitPriceCents
P-77,B-100,BR,BOOK-01,2,3000
P-77,B-100,BR,MUG-02,1,1250

### EIP canonical data model — a marketplace JSON order: canonical order, invoicing request, warehouse CSV
POST {{base}}/eip/canonical/orders/marketplace
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id": "MK-501", "buyer": { "accountId": "A-9" }, "shipping": { "country": "BR" }, "lines": [ { "listing": { "sku": "SKU-BOOK" }, "units": 2, "price": { "amount": "30.00", "currency": "BRL" } }, { "listing": { "sku": "SKU-MUG" }, "units": 1, "price": { "amount": "12.50", "currency": "BRL" } } ] }

### ...the same order as a partner XML purchase order gives the same target documents
POST {{base}}/eip/canonical/orders/partner
Content-Type: application/xml

<PurchaseOrder number="PO-77" currency="BRL"><Customer code="A-9"/><ShipTo country="BR"/><Lines><Line sku="SKU-BOOK" quantity="2" unitPrice="30.00"/><Line sku="SKU-MUG" quantity="1" unitPrice="12.50"/></Lines></PurchaseOrder>

### EIP content filter — invoicing gets only what it needs (no card, contact or cost data)
POST {{base}}/eip/billing/invoice-requests
Content-Type: application/json

{ "orderId": "ORD-3601", "customer": { "id": "CUS-100", "name": "Ana Lima", "email": "ana@example.com", "phone": "+55 11 99999-0000", "taxId": "123.456.789-09", "address": { "street": "Rua A, 1", "city": "Sao Paulo", "country": "BR" } }, "payment": { "method": "CARD", "authorizationCode": "AUTH-777", "card": { "number": "4111111111111111", "holder": "ANA LIMA", "expiry": "12/29" } }, "items": [ { "sku": "SKU-BOOK", "quantity": 2, "unitPrice": 30, "unitCost": 18, "supplier": "SUP-1" } ], "internalNotes": "VIP" }

### What invoicing received
GET {{base}}/eip/invoicing/invoices/ORD-3601

### EIP claim check — check a document in; the archive gets only the claim key (the claim expires after 3 seconds)
POST {{base}}/eip/orders/documents
Content-Type: application/json

{ "orderId": "ORD-3701", "document": { "fileName": "po-3701.pdf", "mediaType": "application/pdf", "contentBase64": "JVBERi0xLjQKJcfsj6IKMSAwIG9iago8PC9UeXBlL0NhdGFsb2c+PgplbmRvYmoK" } }

### Check the document out: replace the key with the claimKey above (404 once it has expired)
GET {{base}}/eip/orders/documents/CLM-replace-with-the-claim-key

### EIP content enricher — the order gains the customer from the CRM
POST {{base}}/eip/orders/enrich
Content-Type: application/json

{ "orderId": "ORD-3801", "customerId": "CUS-100", "items": [ { "sku": "SKU-BOOK", "quantity": 2, "unitPrice": 30 } ] }

### The CRM is down for CUS-DOWN... customers: 503, enrichment FAILED
POST {{base}}/eip/orders/enrich
Content-Type: application/json

{ "orderId": "ORD-3802", "customerId": "CUS-DOWN-1", "items": [ { "sku": "SKU-BOOK", "quantity": 2, "unitPrice": 30 } ] }

### EIP request-reply — synchronous: the requestor waits for the warehouse (waitedMillis >= 300)
POST {{base}}/eip/stock/reservations/sync
Content-Type: application/json

{ "orderId": "ORD-4101", "sku": "SKU-BOOK", "quantity": 2 }

### Asynchronous: 202 PENDING now, the warehouse calls the reply channel later
POST {{base}}/eip/stock/reservations/async
Content-Type: application/json

{ "orderId": "ORD-4102", "sku": "SKU-MUG", "quantity": 1 }

###
GET {{base}}/eip/stock/reservation-replies/ORD-4102

### EIP return address — the invoice goes to the address in X-Reply-To
POST {{base}}/eip/invoice-requests
Content-Type: application/json
X-Reply-To: /eip/requestors/checkout/invoice-replies

{ "orderId": "ORD-4201", "amount": 72.5 }

###
POST {{base}}/eip/invoice-requests
Content-Type: application/json
X-Reply-To: /eip/requestors/backoffice/invoice-replies

{ "orderId": "ORD-4202", "amount": 30 }

###
GET {{base}}/eip/requestors/checkout/invoice-replies

###
GET {{base}}/eip/requestors/backoffice/invoice-replies

### EIP event-driven consumer — processed when it arrives
POST {{base}}/eip/payment-events
Content-Type: application/json

{ "eventId": "EVT-4301", "orderId": "ORD-4301", "type": "PAYMENT_CONFIRMED" }

###
GET {{base}}/eip/payment-events/ORD-4301

### EIP polling consumer — added now, allocated by the next poll (every second)
POST {{base}}/eip/stock/pending-orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "orderId": "ORD-4401" }

###
GET {{base}}/eip/stock/polled-orders

### EIP competing consumers — put work on the list, then run three consumers at once
POST {{base}}/eip/invoice-work/items
Content-Type: application/json

{ "orderIds": ["ORD-4501", "ORD-4502", "ORD-4503", "ORD-4504", "ORD-4505", "ORD-4506"] }

###
POST {{base}}/eip/invoice-work/runs
Content-Type: application/json

{ "consumers": 3 }

###
GET {{base}}/eip/invoice-work/items/ORD-4503

### EIP channel adapter — the legacy ERP's CSV, and the same order through the adapter
GET {{base}}/eip/legacy/orders/ORD-LEGACY-1001

###
GET {{base}}/eip/adapters/legacy-orders/ORD-LEGACY-1001
